expected":"PenetrationBiasClampRetained","id":"C10","overrides":{"penetration_bias_guard":"Triggered"}},{"expected":"UndeclaredPhysicsCallbackBlocked","id":"C11","overrides":{"callback":"Undeclared"}},{"expected":"DeclaredCallbackProfileBoundary","id":"C12","overrides":{"callback":"DeclaredNonEngineeringProfile"}},{"expected":"UndeclaredMeshProviderBlocked","id":"C13","overrides":{"mesh_provider":"Undeclared"}},{"expected":"DeclaredMeshProviderRetained","id":"C14","overrides":{"mesh_provider":"Declared"}},{"expected":"RotationalInertiaApproximationRetained","id":"C15","overrides":{"inertia_subject":"AsymmetricMeanApproximation"}},{"expected":"AdmissibleNoKnownNumericalAnomaly","id":"C16","overrides":{}},{"expected":"HalfSpaceAnalyticalPath","id":"C17","overrides":{"contact_path":"ExactlyOneHalfSpaceAnalytical"}},{"expected":"HalfSpacePairUnsupported","id":"C18","overrides":{"contact_path":"HalfSpaceVsHalfSpace"}},{"expected":"MeshFallbackApproximationRetained","id":"C19","overrides":{"contact_path":"MeshWithoutProviderConvexFallback"}},{"expected":"Q16ProfileDistinct","id":"C20","overrides":{"determinism_profile":"Q16DeterministicNet"}},{"expected":"ReplayConformantOnly","id":"C21","overrides":{"replay":"ExactEnvironmentMatch"}},{"expected":"ReplayMismatchBlocked","id":"C22","overrides":{"replay":"MismatchOrCorrupt"}},{"expected":"InvariantDriftRetained","id":"C23","overrides":{"invariant_drift":"ExceededDeclaredDiagnosticEnvelope"}},{"expected":"UnsupportedPhenomenonBlocked","id":"C24","overrides":{"requested_phenomenon":"Unsupported"}},{"expected":"ModelProfileMismatchBlocked","id":"C25","overrides":{"model_profile_binding":"Mismatch"}},{"expected":"TraceInvarianceBlocked","id":"C26","overrides":{"trace_behavior":"ChangedByTraceLevel"}}],"current_engine_findings":[{"fact":"PhysicsWorld::step accepts f64 dt without an engineering precondition check; the future wrapper must reject zero, negative, and non-finite dt before invoking the ordinary engine.","id":"F01","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"integrator sanitizes non-finite force and torque accumulators to zero before integration; these input sanitizations do not increment NAN_ZEROED_COUNT.","id":"F02","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/integrator.rs"},{"fact":"post-integration non-finite linear/angular velocity is zeroed; non-finite position freezes linear velocity rather than teleporting; NAN_ZEROED_COUNT records these post-state events.","id":"F03","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/integrator.rs"},{"fact":"linear speed is clamped to 1000 and angular speed to 100 inside the ordinary integrator without a per-run anomaly record.","id":"F04","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/integrator.rs"},{"fact":"contact position-correction bias is capped by MAX_BIAS_VELOCITY=10.0.","id":"F05","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"rotational integration uses a scalar mean inverse inertia; source comments state this is exact for isotropic bodies such as spheres and approximate for asymmetric bodies.","id":"F06","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/integrator.rs"},{"fact":"PhysicsCallback can modify forces, impulses, friction, and receive collision/work/dissipation hooks; ordinary step uses NoOpCallback while step_with_callback admits a caller callback.","id":"F07","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"mesh contact behavior is injected through a registered provider; without it, mesh pairs may fall through to generic GJK behavior described in source as a convex-hull approximation.","id":"F08","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"exactly one HalfSpace against a bounded convex support-mapped shape is resolved by the current analytical path and does not fall through to generic GJK/EPA; HalfSpace-vs-HalfSpace remains unsupported.","id":"F09","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"HalfSpace::support itself remains a finite-extent GJK compatibility approximation with HALFSPACE_EXTENT=1e6, but the current world avoids that approximation for exactly-one-HalfSpace pairs.","id":"F10","source":"crates/core/symtropy-math/src/halfspace.rs"},{"fact":"deterministic-net quantizes accumulated forces before integration and positions/linear velocities after integration to Q16.16; it is a distinct numerical profile, not an accuracy claim.","id":"F11","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"},{"fact":"InvariantSnapshot/InvariantDrift measure mass, COM, momentum, energy, speed, rotation errors, penetration and non-finite body count; is_numerically_healthy only checks non-finite bodies and rotation tolerances, not all possible engineering anomalies.","id":"F12","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/diagnostics.rs"},{"fact":"SYMTAPE v1 records a versioned demo world, raw-bit numeric fields, stable NetIds, commands and per-tick WorldSnapshot hashes for 2D/3D/4D; its FNV-1a state hash is a determinism diagnostic, not an engineering evidence commitment.","id":"F13","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/bin/replay_cli.rs"},{"fact":"the current source records a separate ignored ten-box stack solver-scaling problem; a numerically quiet small fixture must not imply arbitrary long-stack applicability.","id":"F14","source":"crates/core/symtropy-physics/src/world.rs"}],"default_disposition":"AdmissibleNoKnownNumericalAnomaly","derivation_priority":[["dt_state",["Zero","Negative","NonFinite"],"InvalidTimeStepBlocked"],["authored_numeric_input",["NaNForce","InfiniteTorque"],"NonFiniteInputBlocked"],["post_state",["NonFinite"],"NonFiniteStateBlocked"],["callback",["Undeclared"],"UndeclaredPhysicsCallbackBlocked"],["mesh_provider",["Undeclared"],"UndeclaredMeshProviderBlocked"],["requested_phenomenon",["Unsupported"],"UnsupportedPhenomenonBlocked"],["model_profile_binding",["Mismatch"],"ModelProfileMismatchBlocked"],["trace_behavior",["ChangedByTraceLevel"],"TraceInvarianceBlocked"],["replay",["MismatchOrCorru